{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/236145-the-most-badass-awesome-epic-moments-of-the-owod-cannon","id":236145,"title":"The most Badass/Awesome/Epic moments of the OWoD Cannon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-20T20:56:30-07:00","id":236145,"title":"The most Badass/Awesome/Epic moments of the OWoD Cannon","content":"Those moments in which you just go &quot;FUCK YEAH!&quot; when you read it or &quot;Holy shit!&quot;. personally, to me it was the final message delivered by Witness1 on Time of Judgement and the post list of Hunter-Net leading to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T05:22:41-07:00","id":236354,"title":"","content":"Whole plot associated with Czar Vargo. FUCKING ZEPPELIN EMPEROR, FUCK YEAH.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T05:52:20-07:00","id":236390,"title":"","content":"The last message from the time of judgement, news ticker<br /> &quot;&quot;There are the blood gods.&quot;<br /> truly awesome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T07:07:36-07:00","id":236437,"title":"","content":"Well I do find much of that opening fiction of the HtR's ToJ section awesome, two most epic for were Leaf's sacrifice (page 105) and soldier91's message (page 109). With Leaf it was the Redeemer signature character going out in the ultimate manner with her mindset and Creed, giving her life to redeem a demon and if you're familiar with the Fallen you know that the nature of the person they come to inhabit affects their nature and it becomes a part of them. So you can imagine the affects of someone like Leaf would have on a Fallen.<br /> <br /> With soldier91's post it is basically what HtR is, at least the way I see it anyway. A hunter sees the full scope of the world around him and just how insignificant he is compared to it all. Naturally its truly crushing for him and he considers ending it all. Pretty much every Imbued reaches that moment at least once, provided they live long enough, where they realize just how vast their fight is and how hopeless it is. Some break under the pressure, others become emboldened. In the end he realizes there's still something he can do even if its a little thing. Let's face the Imbued have no chance in hell at eliminating the global conspiracies of other lines, they're too few, too disorganized and just not powerful or influential enough to even challenge them. The best they can do is the small victories.<br /> <br /> Beyond that I truly loved how Wraith: the Oblivion ended and I consider <i>Ends of Empire</i> to be the best of gameline ending books. The Smiling Lord nuking Enoch and getting rid of one of the more gonzo parts of <i>Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand </i>was enjoyable to say the least even if did go horribly wrong for them all. The war with the Yellow Springs, the Mnemosi Guild Book, the section on the Ferrymen, the return of Charon, learning the ultimate fates of all the major NPCs and so many other parts in the book. But my favorite aspect is the closing fiction, we see Eric, who we've seen through out the 2nd Ed of WtO in his quest to find this other wraith that he fell in love with, finally finds her and it ends with him introducing himself. The OWoD line that's been often considered too dark, too bleak, too depressing and all that ends, after the carnage and chaos of the rest of the book, on a hopeful, positive note.<br /> <br /> Finally the opening of the Introduction section in <i>Guide to the Technocracy</i>. It was the third or fourth book I had read for MtAs and by that point I was fairly certain the Technocracy was MtAs's Pentex, the BSD and the Wyrm, this vast powerful antagonistic force in the universe. The opening fiction of the book did little to change that but then I read the Introduction chapter and my eyes were opened to the Technocracy and that they were more than just mere antagonists. So I got to hand it to the Ivory Tower authors and the Mind Procedures they slipped into the book, they really sell on the idea that of the Union as protagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T09:14:27-07:00","id":237047,"title":"","content":"Czar Vargo was cool I admit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/236145-the-most-badass-awesome-epic-moments-of-the-owod-cannon?p=236390#post236390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last message from the time of judgement, news ticker<br /> &quot;&quot;There are the blood gods.&quot;<br /> truly awesome</div> </div> </div> </div>I have that entire ticker somewhere. It was rather lengthy but I thought it was worth saving.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of moments of awesome, and I thought the endings for the books went out with an impressive bang.<br /> <br /> <b>Brice &quot;Leather' Nads&quot; Hill (1971-??):</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Before vanishing </span></span></i></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">claimed to have personally destroyed over 63 RDs, including </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">6 Nephandi, 3 Marauders, 8 Tradition mages, a pack of werewolves, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">the fomori they were fighting, 7 vampires, 2 Bygones and four unidentified &quot;others.&quot; H was last seen emptying a </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">depleted-uranium shell chain gun at the Paradox manifestation </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Wrinkle, and he has since become the subject of many </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">popular Iterator ballads (written in rhyming C code, or, for </span></span></i></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">a laugh, in Pascal) which suggest that he will one day return from a Paradox Realm bearing Wrinkle's head. Soberer minds however, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">maintain that Wrinkle simply annihilated Hill in </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">an uncharacteristic show of pique.</span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> ~~Guide to the Technocracy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 08-22-2014, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T09:28:02-07:00","id":237073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode